we've been expecting the iPhone 9 the  20/20 iPad pro in other Apple products  to get announced at Apple's annual March  event where Apple usually has new  product releases  however the coronavirus has other plans  I'll explain in just a minute  last year Apple sent out invitations to  their March event on March 11th and now  on march 13th 2020 finally made an  official announcement but not for what  we were expecting  yep they announced their annual WWDC  conference and there are some major  changes this year in the words of Phil  Schiller himself Apple is delivering  WWDC this June as an online experience  for the first time ever that means no  live audience  no hands-on sessions with new products  and no live presentations for developers  everything is happening online so with  that said what does this all mean well  first of all since they didn't  acknowledge their March event a single  time this means that if they were in  fact planning to have a March event it  is now 100% confirmed that it is not  happening this means that any new  hardware releases that Apple was  planning to launch this month including  the iPhone 9 and 20/20 iPad pro are  going to be delayed until their WWDC  event in June yes that means we have to  wait another couple of months for those  product releases and this isn't just my  own personal speculation based on my  opinion check out this quote from Craig  federighi when Apple announced that WWDC  2020 is happening online with all the  new products and technologies we've been  working on WWDC 2020 is going to be big  with Craig adding in that extra little  bit of info Apple is hinting that WWDC  is going to be packing more  announcements and product launches than  usual which most likely includes those  products that were meant to be launched  at their March event so of course we all  know why it happened and that's the  corona virus pandemic Phil Schiller  admitted it himself mentioning that the  current health situation has required  Apple to create a new online WWDC  twenty20 format so now that we know why  it happened let's get into the details  of what went so wrong that  was forced to delay these releases when  the coronavirus broke out in China most  of the factories were completely shut  down right as Apple was going full speed  ahead with the production of iPhone 9  and other new products that means that  the required parts for assembly were not  being manufactured for weeks during  those shutdowns causing supply shortages  and slowdowns it was so bad that  Bloomberg reported that Apple stores are  facing shortages of current iphone parts  and replacements due to the corona virus  there are even rumors that the iPhone 12  meant to launch in September could be  delayed as well yep that's how serious  this is  this is gonna be very bad for Apple  sales and profits this year and this  isn't just affecting Apple everyone is  getting hit including Samsung which  unfortunately released their new S 20  line right before the coronavirus  started getting more serious they even  made a statement blaming much lower  sales of their s 20 phones on the  coronavirus and with the S 20 ultra  being priced at a mass of $1400 not as  many people are gonna be buying in when  there is so much uncertainty over the  world economy during this pandemic there  are already huge numbers of people  getting laid off due to the corona virus  and some are saying that this is just  the beginning with the economy going  down a lot of businesses are starting to  struggle especially ones that sell  expensive luxury devices that people  obviously don't need to survive so for  that reason Apple and many other tech  companies are in trouble and because  less people are buying smart phones and  tech devices there are going to be less  people watching youtube videos trying to  figure out which tech devices to buy  leading to a drop in viewership on many  tech focused YouTube channels like this  one so from all of the tech channels on  YouTube we want to ask you guys to keep  watching videos from your favorite tech  channels and of course other channels  that you enjoy watching to help support  us and help us get through these tough  times as well so with that hopefully you  learn something new from this video and  if you did feel free to click that  circle above to subscribe and check out  the type of tech videos that we make  right over there right here at max tech  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video  [Music]
 

